-- title:
--   Moving the ∞-Igusa ring decentres off-branch good points (q=3)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q = 3$ (hypothesis `hq3`), $M'$ is a non-zero natural number not divisible by $q$ (`hqM'`), and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$ (`hA`). Two function fields of Laurent series occur: $\overline{F} :=$ `fieldBar q M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change `laurentBaseChange` of the rational function field `xHFunctionField (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$; and $\overline{F}_0 :=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the full level-$M'$ modular function field. The hypothesis `hle` asserts $\overline{F}_0 \le \overline{F}$, and `IntermediateField.inclusion hle` denotes the resulting embedding. In characteristic $q$ the field `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` is the subfield of Laurent series over the residue field of $A$ generated by `jqModC` and `jqNModC … M'`.
--
--   **Place data in characteristic $q$.** $W$ is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over `ResidueField A`, and `hW` says that $W$ is exactly `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`: the places $w$ which are rational, are affine geometric places in the sense of the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ at `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q (ResidueField A)`, the set of those $j$ for which every elliptic curve with that $j$-invariant has no non-zero $q$-torsion point over the field.
--
--   **Constant reduction.** $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from $\overline{F}_0$ to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of $\overline{F}_0$ meeting $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ exactly in $A$, a surjective residue homomorphism with kernel the maximal ideal and compatible with $A \to$ `ResidueField A`, the scaling property `exists_smul_mem`, and a degree-preserving place map satisfying the divisor compatibility `mapDomain_placeMap`. The hypothesis `hR₀` says that whenever $y$ is a Laurent series over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-Laurent series lies in $\overline{F}_0$, that element lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over `ResidueField A`, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   **The two families of valuation subrings of $\overline{F}$.** $\zeta$ is an index in `Idx q`, i.e. a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is a family of valuation subrings of $\overline{F}$ indexed by the projective line [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) over $\mathbb Z/q$, and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ a family indexed by $W$. The Igusa group of hypotheses consists of: `hIg_inf`, which identifies $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ at $\infty =$ `lineInfty q` as a Gauss ring, namely $f \in O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ if and only if there are Laurent series $x, y$ over $A$ with the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ non-zero and $f \cdot y = x$ as $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-Laurent series; `hIg`, which for each line $\ell$ provides $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with `redQ q γ • lineInfty q = ℓ` and $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj`, injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$; and `hIg_perm`, that for every index $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ the pullbacks along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permute the family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$. The supersingular group consists of: `hSS_A`, that for each $s \in W$ the subring $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ meets $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ exactly in $A$; `hSS_over`, which for $s \in W$ and $f \in$ `R₀.integers` such that $f$ has non-negative order at every place of $\overline{F}_0$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the element $j :=$ `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` of $\overline{F}_0$ has non-negative order, and such that the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, asserts that the image of $f$ in $\overline{F}$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and that for every $a \in A$ with $\mathrm{residue}_A(a) = s.\mathrm{evalAt}(R_0.\mathrm{residue}(f))$ the difference of that image and $a$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and in its maximal ideal; `hSS_fix`, that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is carried to itself by pullback along every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr`, that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ contains an element $t$ such that $t - a$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and is a unit there for every $a \in A$.
--
--   **Regular prolongation and compatibilities.** $R$ is a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ from $\overline{F}$ to `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` (a valuation subring with surjective residue map of kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$, and with the scaling property), and `hR` says `R.integers` $= O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$; `hR₀O` says that $f \in \overline{F}_0$ lies in `R₀.integers` precisely when its image in $\overline{F}$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$.
--
--   **Uniformiser and constant-field data.** An element $\pi \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ and $\pi \in A$; an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ together with $\pi_0 \in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$, such that $A \cap k_0$ (the `comap` of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), is henselian (`hhens`) and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`), and such that every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$ (`hκ`). Further auxiliary data: a prime $\ell \ge 3$ with $\ell \neq q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   **The finite layer.** $K_1$ is a finite extension of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $A_1$ a valuation subring of $K_1$ with $A_1 = A \cap K_1$ (`hA₁`), which is a discrete valuation ring and henselian local.
--
--   Given all this, and with $\overline{F}$ regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the assertion is the following, for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $\overline{F}/k_0$ subject to four conditions: the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is all of $\overline{F}$; $F_0$ is stable under every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; a linear disjointness condition, namely for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every $m$, every $K'$-linearly independent family $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and every family $a$ of elements of the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces all $a_i = 0$; and $F_0$ contains every element of $\overline{F}$ whose Laurent series lies in the range of `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`, i.e. has rational coefficients.
--
--   Write $T_1$ for the compositum `IntermediateField.adjoin k₀ (algebraMap (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) F̄ '' K₁) ⊔ F₀`. For every $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1$ whose structure map agrees with the inclusion $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to \overline{F}$ on $A_1 \subseteq K_1$, and for every $j_1 \in T_1$ whose image in $\overline{F}$ is the inclusion of the element `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` of $\overline{F}_0$, with $j_1 \neq 0$, consider the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak X_1 :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ T₁ j₁`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of the two affine charts $X_{\mathrm{fin}} = \operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgFin` (the elements of $T_1$ integral over $A_1[j_1]$) and $X_{\infty} = \operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgInf` (integral over $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$), with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$.
--
--   Five predicates are introduced by local definitions. For $x \in \mathfrak X_1$ and $f \in T_1$, `InStalk x f` says that for every point $y$ of either chart mapping to $x$ under the respective morphism `ιFin`, `ιInf` there are chart elements $g, h$ with $h \notin y$ and $f h = g$ in $T_1$; `InMax x f` is the same with the additional requirement $g \in y$. For a place $P$ of $\overline{F}$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, `Centred P x` says that $P$ is rational (the map from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ to its residue field is surjective) and that every $f \in T_1$ with `InStalk x f` satisfies: the image of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$, the value $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ lies in $A$, and the valuation of $A$ at that value is $< 1$ if and only if `InMax x f`. `GoodPt x` is the conjunction of five clauses: `toBase` sends $x$ to the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$; $x$ specialises only to itself; for each point $y$ of the finite chart over $x$, every chart element whose image in $\overline{F}$ is a non-unit of `R.integers` lies in $y$; the same for the chart at infinity; and for each point $y$ of the finite chart over $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the finite chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$ satisfies $\varphi(\mathtt{jChartFin}) \notin$ `ssJSet q Ω`. The predicate `Reads x Q`, for a place $Q$ of `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` over `ResidueField A`, says that every $f \in T_1$ with `InStalk x f` has its image in `R.integers`, with $R$-residue in the valuation subring of $Q$, and lying in the non-units of that subring exactly when `InMax x f`; this predicate does not occur in the conclusion. Finally `OffBranch x` says that for every line $\ell \neq$ `lineInfty q` and every point $y$ of either chart over $x$ there is a chart element whose image in $\overline{F}$ is a non-unit of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ and which does not lie in $y$.
--
--   The conclusion is: for every $g$ in the subgroup of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-automorphisms of $\overline{F}$ generated by the set of level automorphisms $\{\,\tau \mid \exists\, \zeta' \in \mathtt{Idx } q,\ \gamma \in \Gamma_0(M'),\ \tau = \mathtt{levelAutBar } q\ M'\ \zeta'\ \gamma\,\}$, if the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ along $g$ is different from $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$, then for all points $x, x'$ of $\mathfrak X_1$ satisfying `GoodPt` and `OffBranch`, and every place $P$ of $\overline{F}$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, if `Centred P x` holds then `Centred (g • P) x'` fails, where $g \bullet P$ is the transport of $P$ by $g$.
--
--   This is the $q = 3$ case of the statement that a level automorphism which does not preserve the Igusa Gauss ring $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ cannot move a place centred at a good off-branch point of the two-chart integral model to a place centred at another such point; it is the separation property that prevents the branches of the special fibre from being identified. It is used in the construction of the smooth Igusa base model, [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaBaseModel_smoothPointStalks_of_eq_three`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaBaseModel_smoothPointStalks_of_eq_three), on the Igusa-tower leg of the semistable-covering analysis of modular curves in residue characteristic $q$.
